PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Round 1 sharpens prior split: 7 colleagues (1,3-6,8,9) now converge on C (monthly revisions + quarterly distribution breaches 30-day statutory rule while >25 employees on 1 Jan 2023); 3 colleagues (2,7,10) hold for D (2022 threshold of 30 employees triggers electronic-monitoring policy obligation that persists into 2023 despite later drop to 24). 

Core disagreement preserved: whether ESA threshold (ss. 21.1.1–21.1.2, 41.1.1–41.2) is strictly annual/reset (no carry-over of prior violation once below 25 on next 1 Jan) or creates ongoing duty. Secondary point on C: most treat quarterly cadence as automatic 30-day breach; colleague 7 alone suggests possible compliance depending on exact revision/distribution dates. 

A/B/E remain exempt (below 25 on all relevant 1 Jan dates). My prior lean toward C is reinforced by majority view and Ministry guidance on annual re-testing; unresolved question is exact statutory text on persistence of 2022 violations.}

